('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-1',29,'pma-rotation','A square turns 90 degrees clockwise each step, while its corner marker remains attached to the same corner. Which figure follows?', 'HARD','MEDIUM','Square rotated clockwise with marker attached','Square unchanged with marker at center','Square reflected with marker opposite','Square rotated counterclockwise with marker detached','A','The whole marked figure rotates clockwise as one unit; the marker stays at its original relative corner.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-nw','square+dot-ne','square+dot-se','?'],ARRAY['square+dot-sw','square+dot-ne','square+dot-center','square+dot-nw'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-1',30,'pma-matrix-reasoning','The first row combines a horizontal and vertical line into a cross. Apply that overlay rule to the diagonal pair.', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Both diagonals together','Horizontal and vertical lines','One rising diagonal','One falling diagonal','A','The output overlays both input lines. Combining rising and falling diagonals gives an X.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['bar-h','bar-v','bar-h+bar-v','slash','backslash','?'],ARRAY['slash+backslash','bar-h+bar-v','slash','backslash'])),
