('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-1',32,'pma-pattern-completion','The outline gains one side at each step: triangle, square, pentagon. Which outline follows?', 'MEDIUM','HIGH','Hexagon','Square','Triangle','Circle','A','The polygon side count increases by one each step: 3, 4, 5, then 6. The next is a hexagon.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['tri-up','square','pentagon','?'],ARRAY['hexagon','square','tri-up','circle'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-1',33,'pma-mirror-reflection','Reflect an upper-left marker across the rising diagonal mirror line. Where does it appear?', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Lower-right','Upper-right','Lower-left','Center','A','Reflection across the southwest-to-northeast diagonal maps the upper-left corner to the lower-right corner.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-nw','?'],ARRAY['square+dot-se','square+dot-ne','square+dot-sw','square+dot-center'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-1',34,'pma-figure-analogy','The first figure changes by replacing its outer circle with a square while keeping the inner dot fixed. Apply that change to the second figure.', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Square with center dot','Circle with center dot','Square with corner dot','Diamond with center dot','A','The transformation changes only the outer circle to a square; the center dot remains in place.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['circle+dot-center','square+dot-center','circle+dot-nw','?'],ARRAY['square+dot-nw','circle+dot-center','square+dot-center','diamond+dot-center'])),
