('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',22,'pma-pattern-completion','A square’s center marker moves clockwise while its four corner markers stay fixed. Where is the center marker after top, right, bottom?', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Left','Top','Right','Center','A','The center marker follows the cardinal cycle top, right, bottom, then left. The corner markers do not change.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-top','square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-right','square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-bottom','?'],ARRAY['square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-left','square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-top','square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-right','square+dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-center'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',23,'pma-figure-analogy','A large square changes into a small square and a large circle changes into a small circle. Apply the same size rule to a diamond.', 'EASY','MEDIUM','Small diamond','Large diamond','Small square','Small circle','A','The rule changes only size and preserves the outline. A large diamond becomes a small diamond.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square','small-square','circle','small-circle','diamond','?'],ARRAY['small-diamond','diamond','small-square','small-circle'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',24,'pma-odd-figure','Which figure contains a line that does not pass through the center?', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Circle with horizontal diameter','Circle with vertical diameter','Circle with rising diagonal through center','Circle with top-side segment','D','The first three lines pass through the center and form diameters; the final segment sits near the top and misses the center.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY[]::text[],ARRAY['circle+bar-h','circle+bar-v','circle+slash','circle+seg-top-h'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',25,'pma-spatial-reasoning','A marker cycles through the side midpoints in the order right, left, top, bottom. Which position follows?', 'MEDIUM','LOW','Top','Right','Bottom','Left','B','After completing the four-position cycle right, left, top, bottom, it returns to right.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-right','square+dot-left','square+dot-top','square+dot-bottom','?'],ARRAY['square+dot-top','square+dot-right','square+dot-bottom','square+dot-left'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',26,'pma-pattern-completion','The square keeps its outline while one diagonal changes from rising to falling, then back. Which diagonal follows?', 'EASY','MEDIUM','Rising diagonal','Falling diagonal','Horizontal line','Vertical line','A','The two diagonal orientations alternate rising, falling, rising.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+slash','square+backslash','square+slash','?'],ARRAY['square+slash','square+backslash','square+bar-h','square+bar-v'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',27,'pma-matrix-reasoning','A marker at one corner is replaced by a small circle at the opposite corner; the outer shape stays fixed. What is the output for a marker at upper-right?', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Square with small circle at lower-left','Square with small circle at lower-right','Square with small circle at upper-left','Square with marker at upper-right','A','The rule moves the marked corner to its opposite; upper-right maps to lower-left.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-nw','square+small-circle+dot-se','square+dot-ne','?'],ARRAY['square+small-circle+dot-sw','square+small-circle+dot-se','square+small-circle+dot-nw','square+dot-ne'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',28,'pma-figure-series','A diamond’s marker moves clockwise by one vertex each step: top, right, bottom. Where is it next?', 'EASY','MEDIUM','Left','Top','Right','Center','A','The four-vertex sequence proceeds top, right, bottom, left, then repeats.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['diamond+dot-top','diamond+dot-right','diamond+dot-bottom','?'],ARRAY['diamond+dot-left','diamond+dot-top','diamond+dot-right','diamond+dot-center'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',29,'pma-counting-shapes','The number of markers doubles: one center marker, then two opposite markers, then four corner markers. Which figure has eight markers?', 'HARD','LOW','Six markers: four corners and top/bottom','Eight markers: four corners and four side midpoints','Four corner markers','Five markers: four corners and center','B','Four corner markers double to eight by adding a marker at each of the four side midpoints.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['dot-center','dot-top+dot-bottom','dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw','?'],ARRAY['dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-top+dot-bottom','dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-top+dot-right+dot-bottom+dot-left','dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw','dot-nw+dot-ne+dot-se+dot-sw+dot-center'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',30,'pma-figure-analogy','A large outline becomes a small outline and its center marker stays unchanged. Apply the change to a hexagon with a center marker.', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Small hexagon with center marker','Large hexagon with center marker','Small hexagon without marker','Small diamond with center marker','A','Only the outline shrinks; the hexagon type and center marker are preserved.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-center','small-square+dot-center','hexagon+dot-center','?'],ARRAY['small-hexagon+dot-center','hexagon+dot-center','hexagon','diamond+dot-center'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',31,'pma-odd-figure','Which figure has a marker that is not at a corner or the center?', 'MEDIUM','LOW','Square with upper-left dot','Square with center dot','Square with right-side dot','Square with lower-right dot','C','The upper-left and lower-right markers are corners, and one is centered. The right-side marker lies midway along an edge.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY[]::text[],ARRAY['square+dot-nw','square+dot-center','square+dot-right','square+dot-se'])),
('pma-non-verbal-intelligence-test-3',32,'pma-spatial-reasoning','A marker moves from a corner to the midpoint of the adjacent side, then to the next corner clockwise. From upper-left, which point follows?', 'MEDIUM','MEDIUM','Top-side midpoint','Upper-right corner','Right-side midpoint','Center','A','Moving clockwise from upper-left first reaches the midpoint of the top side before the upper-right corner.',pg_temp.pma_visual(ARRAY['square+dot-nw','?'],ARRAY['square+dot-top','square+dot-ne','square+dot-right','square+dot-center'])),
